Use io and list.

Let heights be a list of 0, 1, 0, 2, 1, 0, 1, 3, 2, 1, 2, and 1.
Let n be count of heights.
Let highest start at 0.
Let left_max be an empty list of whole numbers.
For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    Let value be list_get(address of heights, i).
    If value is more than highest:
        Set highest to value.
    push highest to address of left_max.

Let right_max be an empty list of whole numbers.
For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    push 0 to address of right_max.
Set highest to 0.
For every step from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    Let i be n - 1 - step.
    Let value be list_get(address of heights, i).
    If value is more than highest:
        Set highest to value.
    list_set(address of right_max, i, highest).

Let water start at 0.
For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    Let left be list_get(address of left_max, i).
    Let right be list_get(address of right_max, i).
    Let boundary be left.
    If right is less than boundary:
        Set boundary to right.
    Let depth be boundary - list_get(address of heights, i).
    If depth is more than 0:
        Add depth to water.

Say water.
list_free(address of right_max).
list_free(address of left_max).
list_free(address of heights).
Return 0.
